# --change selects a single change folder even when others would fail.
#
# The refine-stage delta is now the owned YAML source (spec.yaml), validated
# against the published spec-delta JSON Schema — so a delta that violates the
# schema is reported as an error naming the offending JSON path. The old
# markdown-only "unrecognized section heading" warning has no structured-YAML
# analog (the model has no section headings a requirement can be orphaned
# under); JSON Schema validation supersedes it, so this script asserts the
# schema-validation error path instead of that retired warning.

# Without --change, both change folders are checked and the broken one
# fails the run: its proposal is missing an issue AND its spec.yaml delta
# violates the schema (an op outside the allowed set).
exitcode 1 lifecycle validate --stage refine
stdout 'broken.*proposal\.md.*missing a non-empty "issue" field'
stdout 'broken.*spec\.yaml.*schema validation failed at "/deltas/0/op"'

# With --change, only the named (well-formed) folder is checked, and it
# validates clean — exit 0, no errors, no warnings.
exitcode 0 lifecycle validate --stage refine --change well-formed
stdout 'validate: 1 change\(s\), 0 error\(s\), 0 warning\(s\)'

-- openspec/changes/well-formed/proposal.md --
---
issue: "kentra-io/kafka-dq#7"
---

# Title

## Why
x

## What Changes
- x

## Impact
- x

-- openspec/changes/well-formed/specs/auth/spec.yaml --
capability: auth
deltas:
  - op: ADDED
    requirement:
      name: Password login
      text: The system SHALL allow login.
      scenarios:
        - name: ok
          given:
            - a
          when:
            - b
          then:
            - c

-- openspec/changes/broken/proposal.md --
---
issue: ""
---

# Title

## Why
x

## What Changes
- x

## Impact
- x

-- openspec/changes/broken/specs/auth/spec.yaml --
capability: auth
deltas:
  - op: NOTES
    requirement:
      name: Orphaned op
      text: The system SHALL be rejected by the schema.
      scenarios:
        - name: ok
          given:
            - a
          when:
            - b
          then:
            - c
